      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. but when you look at the data on stuff like venture capital and how much new startups actually succeed nowadays, doesn't it seem like the \"efficiency\" argument is kind of a stretch? it feels like most of these big companies just buy out any potential competitors before they even get off the ground, which definitely makes the innovation side look a lot more questionable.",
